"money": -0.26}, "rating_margin": -14.6, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.15, "baseline_margin": -10.79, "analyst_adjustment": -0.21, "key_factors": ["Strong Republican district (R+11 partisan lean) with incumbent Jack Bergman running", "Expert ratings overwhelmingly Safe/Solid R, with only two Likely R", "Prediction markets price Bergman near 88% to win", "Callie Barr has raised competitively ($1.5M) in a rematch but faces a steep structural deficit"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point firmly to Bergman: an R+11 district, incumbency, and a consensus of Safe or Solid R ratings, with markets pricing his win odds near 88 percent. Barr's solid fundraising and the expanded-battlefield chatter justify only a modest nudge toward competitiveness, not a change in category.", "watch": "Any credible general-election polling showing Barr within single digits, or major outside spending into the district, would signal a genuine opening.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Jack Bergman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Northern Michigan's sprawling first district has been reliably Republican, and incumbent Jack Bergman is seeking another term after easily defeating Callie Barr in 2024. Barr is back for a rematch and has run a serious campaign, raising about $1.5 million, and some coverage notes Democrats trying to expand the 2026 battlefield into this district. But the structural math remains difficult: the district leans Republican by roughly eleven points, and Bergman holds the advantages of incumbency and a fundraising edge in total receipts.\n\nNo public general-election polling is available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets. Nearly every professional rater places the race in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Barr only about a one-in-ten chance. The forecast expects Bergman to win by a double-digit margin, with meaningful uncertainty given the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0479, "margin": -11.4}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0291, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0616, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0563, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0433, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0528, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0342, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0842, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0576, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0467, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0524, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0656, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0535, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0526, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0597, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.043, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0523, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.0619, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.0568, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-17", "p_dem": 0.051, "margin": -11.0}]}